Now I understand the codebase. I need to add to GET /v1/objects/{cid}, GET /v1/blocks/{cid}, and GET /v1/gateway/{cid}/{path...}:

1. Conditional caching: strong ETag = `"<cid>"` (double-quoted full CID — object CID for objects, block CID for blocks, final object CID for gateway). If-None-Match with weak comparison: `*`, single tag, comma-separated tags → 304 with no body, evaluated before Range. Unparseable If-None-Match → 400 invalid_request. Other conditional headers (If-Modified-Since etc.) — no new semantics.

2. Single range requests: `Range: bytes=...` — closed interval, suffix, or from-start. 206 with Content-Range and Content-Length. 416 with `range_not_satisfiable` and `Content-Range: bytes */<full length>` for: non-bytes unit, invalid syntax, multiple ranges, start out of bounds, end < start, zero-length suffix, or any range on empty body. End beyond end or suffix beyond body truncates to body bounds. Full-body range still returns 206.

3. HEAD support: same validation as GET, ignores Range, returns status/ETag/Accept-Ranges/Content-Type/Content-Length as GET would (full length), no body ever; If-None-Match match still returns 304.

